# //// Neoffice — un-ignored (upstream ignores public/desk). Commit-the-build: the
# //// SPA is compiled by our build-frontend workflow and committed, because
# //// `bench build` running `yarn build` on a 4 GB tenant gets OOM-killed. An
# //// instance therefore pulls the compiled assets and never builds anything.
# //// Artifacts are listed in NEOFFICE_FORK_MARKERS.md — at the merge, drop them
# //// from the resolution and let the workflow rebuild from the merged sources.
# 2026-05-07 (NORA #28) — frontend build outputs are committed on this branch.
# See docs/COMMIT-BUILD-PATTERN.md in neoffice-devops.
# (helpdesk writes vite output to public/desk/, not public/frontend/.)
# helpdesk/public/desk
helpdesk/public/frontend
helpdesk/public/node_modules
# //// Neoffice — un-ignored (upstream ignores it). Frappe serves the SPA shell from
# //// www/helpdesk/index.html; it is generated from the vite build, so it has to be
# //// committed alongside public/desk/ for an instance that never runs yarn build.
# helpdesk/www/helpdesk/index.html
desk/components.d.ts
# //// Neoffice — repaired entry. Upstream had "desk/stats.html" as the LAST line
# //// with no trailing newline; our commit b713b86fd ("chore: add CLAUDE.md to
# //// gitignore") appended "CLAUDE.md" straight onto it, so from that day NEITHER
# //// path was ignored. Upstream's entry is restored below, on its own line.
# //// "CLAUDE.md" is deliberately NOT re-added: that file carries the branch and
# //// commit-the-build conventions of this fork, it is listed as ours in
# //// NEOFFICE_FORK_MARKERS.md, and it stays tracked — ignoring it would only hide
# //// it from the next clone. At the merge, keep upstream's "desk/stats.html".
desk/stats.html
